# Docker build context filter for the repo root.
#
# The web image is built with the REPO ROOT as its context (it needs
# pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml and the contracts-artifacts sibling),
# so this file is the only thing standing between `docker build` and a layer
# containing every private key in the working tree. Keep the secret rules at
# the top and do not reorder them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. .env and .env.mainnet hold DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY,
# NUVEM_ATTESTER_PRIVATE_KEY, TRADING_OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY and the drill keys.
# A COPY that captured them would bake them into an image layer permanently,
# where they survive any later RUN rm. All runtime config is injected as
# environment variables instead -- see docs/runbooks/DEPLOYMENT_WEB.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEY MATERIAL OUTSIDE .env. THIS SECTION ALSO FAILED ONCE.
#
# docker-compose.yml tells the operator, in the recommended key-handling path:
#
#     printf '%s' 0x<attester-private-key> > secrets/attester.key
#
# at the REPO ROOT -- which is this build context. Until these rules existed the
# file was copied straight into a layer: proven by building a probe image over
# this context, which found /ctx/secrets/attester.key. So the runbook's own
# preferred, most-secure path was the one that leaked the attester key.
#
# The attester key signs the profit measurement every settlement is built on.
# An image carrying it, pushed anywhere, hands that signing authority away
# permanently -- `RUN rm` in a later layer does not remove it.
#
# By directory, and by shape for anything written somewhere unanticipated.
secrets/
**/secrets/
*.key
**/*.key
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
# The keystore/mnemonic shapes a signer tool might leave behind.
*.keystore
**/*.keystore
mnemonic.txt
**/mnemonic.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE KEEPER'S SETTLED-WINDOW STORE. @nuvem/keeper records every settlement it
# has made. It must never enter a build context. Baked into an image layer it
# would mean every container started from that image begins life believing a
# history it did not verify, and SHARING it -- which is precisely how the same
# profit gets settled twice. It also is, literally, the operator's realized
# trading-profit history: an image pushed to any registry publishes it. In a
# deployment it lives on the named volume nuvem-keeper-state; see
# docs/runbooks/ATTESTER.md.
#
# THIS SECTION FAILED ONCE ALREADY, so read the naming carefully before editing.
# The previous rule was `**/keeper-state`, which does NOT match the actual
# default directory `.keeper-state` (LEADING DOT -- packages/keeper-old/src/config.ts
# falls back to ".keeper-state" when NUVEM_KEEPER_STATE_DIR is unset). Every
# operator who had ever run `pnpm --dir packages/keeper-old tick` on the build host
# shipped their journal inside the image. The only reason the current
# nuvem-keeper:local is clean is that no such directory existed when it was
# built. Do not rely on that again.
#
# TWO INDEPENDENT LAYERS, on purpose:
#
#   (1) THE DIRECTORY, under every name it can have. This is the contract, and
#       it is what actually holds. The store is created relative to the PROCESS
#       CWD, which is whatever directory the CLI was launched from -- the repo
#       root, packages/keeper-old, or anywhere else -- so every rule is anchored
#       with `**/` as well as bare.
#   (2) THE FILES INSIDE IT, by shape. Pure defence in depth for the case where
#       someone points NUVEM_KEEPER_STATE_DIR at a directory nobody anticipated.
#       Layer (2) is a backstop; never let it become the only thing catching a
#       state directory.
#
# The store is MIGRATING FROM JSONL TO node:sqlite (packages/keeper-old/src/ledger.ts,
# owned elsewhere), so both shapes are covered, including SQLite's sidecars:
# `-wal` and `-shm` in WAL mode and `-journal` in rollback mode are separate
# files, and a `.sqlite` shipped without its `-wal` is a torn database, which is
# a worse failure than shipping neither.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# (1) The state directory, every name.
.keeper-state
**/.keeper-state
keeper-state
**/keeper-state
packages/keeper-old/state
packages/keeper-old/**/state

# (2) Store files by shape, wherever they landed.
#
# `**/*.jsonl` is now blanket rather than keeper-scoped. The old comment argued
# a JSONL test fixture elsewhere in the workspace was worth keeping; that trade
# is not worth making for an image whose only two consumers (@nuvem/web,
# @nuvem/keeper) read no .jsonl at all. If one is ever genuinely needed, add a
# `!` re-include for that exact path -- do not widen this back out.
*.jsonl
**/*.jsonl
*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-journal
# NARROWED FROM `**/journal-*`, which also matched packages/keeper-old/src/
# journal-store.ts and silently kept a SOURCE FILE out of the image. The build
# then failed inside the container with "Cannot find module ./journal-store.js"
# while typechecking fine on the host — the worst shape of this class of bug,
# because the host says everything is fine.
#
# The keeper's journal files are named by ledger.ts as `keeper-<slug>.db` and its
# SQLite siblings, all of which the patterns above already cover. This one only
# needs to catch a rollback journal sitting beside a database.
**/*-journal
**/snapshot-*.json
**/ledger-*.sqlite*
**/ledger-*.db*
# The ledger's advisory lock file, named exactly this by ledger.ts. NOT a
# blanket `**/*.lock`: that would also swallow packages/contracts/foundry.lock,
# and quietly dropping an unrelated tracked file from the context is the class
# of surprise this file exists to prevent.
**/keeper.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed / generated trees. Never ship the host's node_modules: pnpm's
# store is symlink-based and host-absolute, so copying it in produces
# dangling links and MODULE_NOT_FOUND at boot.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.next
**/out
**/cache
**/broadcast
**/coverage

# Workspace build output is excluded, WITH ONE DELIBERATE EXCEPTION.
# @nuvem/contracts-artifacts/dist is the only committed build product the
# image consumes: Foundry is not installed in the container and the export
# script cannot regenerate it there (it reads packages/contracts/out, which
# is itself excluded above and gitignored). See the runbook.
**/dist
!packages/contracts-artifacts/dist
!packages/contracts-artifacts/dist/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Solidity toolchain inputs the web image has no use for. packages/contracts
# is filtered out of the install; lib/ is a git submodule that may not even
# be initialised in a CI or Railway clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/contracts/lib
packages/contracts/.openzeppelin
packages/contracts/deployments

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo furniture irrelevant to the build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitmodules
.github
.agents
.claude
docs
*.log
*.md
!packages/*/README.md
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Solana lab. scripts/.local holds the attester and drill keypairs -- the
# same never-in-a-layer rule as the .env files above. target/ is gigabytes of
# Rust build output of which images need exactly one committed file (the IDL);
# test-ledger is a local validator's disk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/solana-lab-old/program/scripts/.local
packages/solana-lab-old/program/target/*
!packages/solana-lab-old/program/target/idl
packages/solana-lab-old/program/test-ledger
packages/solana-lab-old/program/.anchor
